a=json.loads((out/'gateway-1.0.1-audit.json').read_text());sizes=a['sizes'];base='https://sarattha.github.io/relayna-gateway/assets/releases/v1.0.1/'
lines=['# v1.0.1 release benchmark','', 'Status: **measurement and evidence audit complete**. Fresh validation measured the committed v1.0.1 runtime on 26 October 2026 (UTC). Final-head CI and GitHub merge gates still apply.','', 'The six full adaptive searches completed **212 fresh-pod trials**, including three HTTP-clean confirmations for each selected setting. OOM exploration and all transport failures remain in the evidence. These finite observations are not production slot recommendations.','', '## Runtime, harness and conditions','', '- Runtime and harness commit: `52c56f9104f43cb108b7ccd647f6911433f8dcfe`; clean checkout. It includes Manrope, monitoring readability fixes, Pingora 0.9.0 and the dependency-only compression patch. Later documentation/evidence commits do not change these measured build inputs.','- Native Linux **amd64** for the host, Docker, image and kind nodes; no emulation. Each size used a separate GitHub-hosted Ubuntu 24.04.5 runner, with four virtual CPUs and approximately 15.62 GiB Docker memory. CPU models differ below; these are not one homogeneous hardware cohort. Exact Docker resources, kernel/version and node identities are in the audit JSON.','- Two Gateway pods, **2 CPUs / 1 GiB memory / 512 MiB serialized-body budget per pod**, glibc mmap threshold 128 KiB, real PostgreSQL/Redis and direct pod endpoints. No production credentials or prompts are used.','- Full adaptive search for 5, 10, 20, 40, 80 and 100 MiB JSON, three fresh-pod trials per confirmed setting. Final offered cohort is **2,048 simultaneous requests per pod**. Initial cohorts vary by body size and expand during discovery; raw rows retain the actual offered cohort.','- Upstream pauses reads for ten seconds and delays its response for two seconds after upload. Each size uses a 180-second client deadline, 300-second condition deadline and 600-second outer trial deadline. The criterion is resource stability, not a latency SLO.','- Each workflow builds the same committed source with `--build`. The resolved image IDs differ across independent builds and are recorded individually. The benchmark builder labels the revision but leaves its image version label `unknown`; Cargo source version is 1.0.1. These source-built images are not the subsequently signed release image.','', 'The workflow dispatch for each size was equivalent to:','', '```sh','scripts/bench-body-admission --json doctor','scripts/bench-body-admission --json run --build \\','  --body-mib <5|10|20|40|80|100> --repetitions 3 \\','  --output target/body-capacity','```','', '### Per-size provenance','', '| JSON MiB | CPU model | Docker memory bytes | Initial → final offered/pod | Trials | Workflow |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
for s in sizes:
 r=s['provenance'];lines.append(f"| {s['body_mib']} | {r['preflight']['host']['cpu_model']} | {r['preflight']['docker']['MemTotal']} | {s['initial_cohort_per_pod']} → {s['cohort_per_pod']} | {s['total_trials']} | [run {s['workflow_id']}](https://github.com/sarattha/relayna-gateway/actions/runs/{s['workflow_id']}) |")
lines+=['','| JSON MiB | Resolved native image ID |','| --- | --- |']
