lines+=['','The full harness directory is retained in both raw archives. Key execution hashes:','']
for k,v in sizes[0]['provenance']['harness_sha256'].items():lines.append(f'- `{k}`: `{v}`.')
lines+=['','## Repeated resource observations','','Memory is the largest individual-pod observation across the three selected trials. Headroom is 1,024 MiB minus the observed cgroup peak. Every selected trial has zero OOMs, restarts, transport errors, scrape errors and admission counter gaps; reservations drain to zero.','', '| JSON MiB | Slots/pod (3/3 clean) | Interpretation | Adjacent slots: OOM trials | Peak RSS / cgroup MiB | Headroom MiB |','| --- | ---: | --- | --- | ---: | ---: |']
for s in sizes:lines.append(f"| {s['body_mib']} | {s['slots']} | {s['label']} | {s['adjacent_slots']}: {s['adjacent_oom_trials']}/{s['adjacent_trials']} | {s['rss_peak_mib']:.2f} / {s['cgroup_peak_mib']:.2f} | {s['headroom_mib']:.2f} |")
lines+=['','The original automated reports label all six results as edges under their observed-adjacent-OOM rule. This independent audit uses a stricter interpretation: **only 100 MiB has OOM in all three adjacent trials**. The other sizes remain tested lower bounds because adjacent OOMs are intermittent. Original observations and reports are retained unchanged; the published audited report applies this interpretation.','', '**The 20 MiB setting reached the 1,024 MiB cgroup peak with zero observed headroom**, despite surviving all three selected trials. Other selected settings also approach the pod limit. These settings must not replace the released defaults of eight slots and 512 MiB; choose deployment-specific headroom. The serialized-byte budget excludes JSON analysis, connection state, allocations and other process memory. Configured slots do not preallocate bodies.','', '## Timing and outcomes','','Latency columns are the worst per-trial percentiles across the three selected trials, in seconds. They are not pooled percentiles. Elapsed is the longest batch duration. Outcome ranges span both pods per trial. All selected HTTP 200 bodies were verified, and HTTP 503 responses used the expected `gateway_overloaded` admission response.','', '| JSON MiB | Success p50 / p95 / p99 s | Rejection p50 / p95 / p99 s | Elapsed s | Verified 200/trial | HTTP 503/trial | Transport / OOM / restarts |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
for s in sizes:
 lat=' / '.join(f"{s['success_latency_worst_ms'][k]/1000:.2f}" for k in ['p50','p95','p99']);den=' / '.join(f"{s['rejection_latency_worst_ms'][k]/1000:.2f}" for k in ['p50','p95','p99'])
 lines.append(f"| {s['body_mib']} | {lat} | {den} | {s['elapsed_max_ms']/1000:.2f} | {'–'.join(map(str,s['success_range']))} | {'–'.join(map(str,s['denial_range']))} | 0 / 0 / 0 |")
t=a['totals'];lines+=['',f"Across all **{t['trials']} exploration and confirmation trials**, there were **{t['successes']:,} verified HTTP 200s**, **{t['503s']:,} admission HTTP 503s**, and **{t['transport_errors']:,} transport errors**. There were {t['resource_stable_trials']} resource-stable trials, {t['http_clean_trials']} HTTP-clean trials, {t['oom_trials']} OOM trials and {t['restarts']} Gateway restarts ({t['oom_pods']} OOM pod observations). These totals retain intentional overload/resource-boundary failures; they do not describe the clean selected settings. No other HTTP status, failed warmup, incomplete trial or non-resource failed trial was found. One surviving exploration trial lost a transport reply and remains HTTP-unclean. Failed-trial memory may be censored by process death; absent/censored measurements remain explicit in raw rows. Owned clusters were cleaned by the workflow.",'', '## Separate fixed-slot latency sanity runs','','The candidate and released v1.0.0 each completed three fresh-pod 5 MiB trials at eight slots/pod, 16 offered requests/pod and the same pod caps, ten-second read pause and two-second response delay. **They ran on different CPU models, so this is not a matched performance experiment. No latency delta, regression threshold or speedup is claimed.** End-to-end latency includes upload, scheduling and the deliberate upstream delay; it is not isolated proxy overhead.','', '| Arm | CPU | Worst trial success p50 / p95 / p99 ms | Verified 200 / admission 503 (3 trials) | Errors / OOM / restarts |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | --- |']
for arm in a['latency']:
 ts=arm['trials'];lat=' / '.join(f"{max(t['success_latency_ms'][k] for t in ts):.2f}" for k in ['p50','p95','p99']);lines.append(f"| {arm['arm']} | {arm['provenance']['preflight']['host']['cpu_model']} | {lat} | {sum(t['successes'] for t in ts)} / {sum(t['statuses'].get('503',0) for t in ts)} | 0 / 0 / 0 |")
lines+=['','- Baseline image index: `ghcr.io/sarattha/relayna-gateway@sha256:20a17e64b435abac5f8fa41c469969b2d7871af275f8686fa7732cb3f9bf4d21`; resolved image ID `sha256:b50d5a24709ca395f28f928eeb41b95a6be99919a0e4b29289ea0ec00e492337`; image source commit `e5200b662a7c1a3d085c00f56bf8ed09c1293f88`.','- Candidate image ID: `sha256:ca7e4da6568392ce4ce47842a7d3a2f83abde6aaa62993ead76f312b1888e2dd`; source commit `52c56f9104f43cb108b7ccd647f6911433f8dcfe`.','- Both runs use the recorded current harness. Their complete provenance, trials and separate workflow links are in the audit and workflow JSON.','', 'The preceding [v1.0.0 resource study](v1.0.0.md) used native ARM64 on Apple M1 Pro with different host resources and a different 5 MiB cohort. Its slot limits and latency are not directly comparable to these amd64 runs. These observations establish fresh version-attributable evidence, not a release-to-release regression claim.','', '## Verification and retained evidence','','The full local verification stack passed: fmt, Clippy, workspace tests, nine upstream header-codec tests, audit/deny/machete, 479 Nextest tests, Trivy, gitleaks and Semgrep. UI build/tests, TypeScript, 56 React tests, artwork/font checks, strict docs and metadata checks passed. The [candidate CI run](https://github.com/sarattha/relayna-gateway/actions/runs/40364043763) passed, including the required continuous 600-second mixed HTTP/SSE/WebSocket and concurrent Usage monitoring check. Later documentation commits must pass their final-head checks before merge. No 24-hour soak is claimed.','', 'Evidence is stored outside the application source tree in an immutable artifact-only Git archive, then copied into documentation hosting with SHA-256 verification. GitHub release attachments remain only the changelog and SPDX SBOM.','', '- [Interactive audited report]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-benchmarks.html), [audited JSON]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-benchmarks.json), [all trial rows CSV]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-trials.csv).','- [Full audit and provenance]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-audit.json), [workflow identities and outcomes]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-workflows.json).','- [Raw resource evidence]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-resource-evidence.tar.gz), [separate latency evidence]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-latency-evidence.tar.gz), [checksums]('+base+'gateway-1.0.1-evidence-SHA256SUMS).','', 'Raw archives retain observations, checkpoints, original HTML/JSON/CSV, failed trials, logs, per-pod memory, hardware/image provenance and exact harness source. Numeric observations are unchanged. Credential scanning passed; kubeconfigs, production keys, tokens and prompts are excluded. The interactive report embeds the same licensed Manrope face as the console.','']
Path('docs/benchmarks/v1.0.1.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
